# Ford Consul Mk I four-door saloon, 1951-1956.
#
# The four-cylinder member of the 1951 Consul / Zephyr Six range, with unitary
# construction and MacPherson-strut front suspension, both new to a British
# Ford. 227,732 built. The Carbodies convertible and Abbott estate are
# different bodies and are not modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Consul
#
# Dimensions 4.166 x 1.626 m, wheelbase 2.540 m. Saloon height was not
# established; the 61 in figure belongs to the convertible.
#
# Shape reference: a black 1954 Consul in true level side elevation, front
# three-quarter and rear three-quarter, all one car. The waist-level chrome
# strip, round lamps, horizontal grille and rounded boot govern.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the period Ford dealer leaflet 'Ford Sets The Fashion'
# (1953-54 season), which names the Consul saloon colours: Edinburgh Green,
# Bristol Fawn, Dorchester Grey, Winchester Blue, Canterbury Green and Black.
# Four are used. Weights 12, 10, 10, 8, total 40, provisional.
#
# Speed 130 km/h. Comfort 50/405, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 50. Class 2.
# Dates are road presence: 1951 intro, retires staggered 1970-1973.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-consul-mk1.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/ford-consul-mk1.dae. References:
# citycars/references/ford-consul-mk1/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: neither front photograph verifies the tail, so it is
# simplified; the bumper wrap and the waist-level chrome strip are not fully
# reproduced. The model height of 1.55 m is an estimate. At 128 px the rounded
# three-box body, vertical-bar grille and round lamps read as a Consul Mk I.


obj=citycar
